__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# Anchored to the repo root ON PURPOSE. An unanchored `data/` also matches
# src/sol_execbench/core/data/ and tests/sol_execbench/core/data/, and in
# session 1 it silently excluded the vendored data-model package from the
# commit -- the code imported it, the working tree had it, and git did not.
# See STATE.md deviation D6.
/data/
artifacts/**/logs/
# Golden reference tensors: 143 GB of regenerable float64 CPU output.
# `scripts/gen_golden.py` rebuilds them from the dataset on any machine, with
# no GPU. The per-workload report beside them IS tracked, because which tier
# produced each golden (float64 vs native_cpu) is a finding, not data.
artifacts/golden/*.pt
# The reduced harness tree each agent sweep verifies against. A derived copy of
# src/ and a few scripts, rebuilt by task_packet.build_verify_root on demand;
# committing it would duplicate the source tree once per run.
artifacts/10/runs/*/verify-root/
# Scratch an agent left in its packet. The solution.json and its declared
# sources ARE tracked -- they are the result -- but the debug scripts, probes and
# local test harnesses an agent wrote along the way are not, and they arrive with
# unpredictable names.
#
# Unpredictable names is exactly why this has to be an allowlist. The previous rule
# excluded only __pycache__, so the stated intent above was never actually enforced
# and scratch accumulated: bt2.py, v_atomic.py, exp1.py, _sweep_ds.py, sweep_at.py.
#
# What must stay: solution.json together with every path it declares in `sources`.
# solution.json ships those with `content: ""`, so the file sitting in the packet is
# the ONLY copy of the result -- dropping it would discard the very thing the run
# produced. The declared paths across all runs to date are kernel.py, gn_triton.py,
# candidate.py, flash_attn.py, tunable.csv and sitecustomize.py; the last is a
# rejected reward-hack vector, kept because a rejected submission still has to be
# auditable. `.attempts.json` stays because it is the agent's own record of what it
# tried, which nothing else reproduces.
#
# The packet SCAFFOLDING is excluded for the same reason verify-root above is:
# definition.json, reference.py, workload.jsonl, TASK.md, ./verify and .packet.json
# are rebuilt by task_packet.py from the committed dataset plus the artifacts/05
# tolerances, and committing them duplicates that material once per problem per
# harness -- 391 copies, ~11 MB per run, growing with every run.
artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/*
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/.attempts.json
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/solution.json
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/kernel.py
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/gn_triton.py
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/candidate.py
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/flash_attn.py
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/tunable.csv
!artifacts/10/runs/*/*/*/packet/sitecustomize.py
*.so
.venv/
uv.lock
.uv-cache/
